1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,920
 Now, in the previous few lectures, we discussed about the planning capability of AI agent

2
00:00:04,920 --> 00:00:07,120
 that we looked at tools and action.

3
00:00:07,120 --> 00:00:13,560
 Now, let us go ahead and discuss in more detail the memory capability of AI agents.

4
00:00:13,560 --> 00:00:18,020
 And there could be two types of memory that it can possess, one is the shorter memory

5
00:00:18,020 --> 00:00:20,120
 and other is the long term memory.

6
00:00:20,120 --> 00:00:27,160
 So, now, remember that AI agents are driven by large language models and large language

7
00:00:27,160 --> 00:00:29,280
 models are stateless.

8
00:00:29,280 --> 00:00:35,400
 They have no memory, so let us say if I send a request to an agent driven by a large

9
00:00:35,400 --> 00:00:38,360
 language model and let us say it gives me a response.

10
00:00:38,360 --> 00:00:43,240
 Now, let us say as a follow up question which has a context to the first query that I had

11
00:00:43,240 --> 00:00:44,240
 sent.

12
00:00:44,240 --> 00:00:51,360
 But for a large language model, it has no memory, it is stateless, so it would not remember

13
00:00:51,360 --> 00:00:53,480
 what was the previous context.

14
00:00:53,480 --> 00:00:59,480
 Now, to overcome this challenge, AI agents have short term memory.

15
00:00:59,480 --> 00:01:06,600
 Now, in the short term memory, agents retain the conversation and the user input during

16
00:01:06,600 --> 00:01:08,200
 the particular session.

17
00:01:08,200 --> 00:01:16,080
 So, whatever interaction happens with the user and AI agent, that is retain for the particular

18
00:01:16,080 --> 00:01:19,000
 session duration.

19
00:01:19,000 --> 00:01:25,920
 First we have the long term memory, the long term memory allows AI agents to retain conversation

20
00:01:25,920 --> 00:01:28,440
 across all previous interactions.

21
00:01:28,440 --> 00:01:34,360
 Now, let us say I am a user and I had an interaction with the travel agent in the month

22
00:01:34,360 --> 00:01:36,560
 of January 2024.

23
00:01:36,560 --> 00:01:41,600
 Then next, I have another conversation in the month of March 2024.

24
00:01:41,600 --> 00:01:48,560
 So, what it will do is, so for all the previous interaction, it will summarize the conversation

25
00:01:48,560 --> 00:01:50,440
 and then store it.

26
00:01:50,440 --> 00:01:56,560
 So, next time, let us say in September 2024, when I have a conversation with the agent,

27
00:01:56,560 --> 00:02:02,120
 it is going to load all the previous interactions that have been summarized.

28
00:02:02,120 --> 00:02:10,600
 So, now, in most cases, you can store all the previous interactions between 1 to 365 days.

29
00:02:10,600 --> 00:02:16,040
 And remember, most of the time, it is not the entire conversation that is stored, but it

30
00:02:16,040 --> 00:02:19,240
 is a summary of that interaction.

31
00:02:19,240 --> 00:02:23,160
 Now, let us try and understand the short term memory through an example.

32
00:02:23,160 --> 00:02:28,080
 Now, let us say, we have a user Joe, who is planning a two week scheme vacation.

33
00:02:28,080 --> 00:02:34,360
 So, once the user starts interacting with the AI agent, the first thing it does is, in the

34
00:02:34,360 --> 00:02:39,360
 short term memory, it will create a session ID for that particular interaction.

35
00:02:39,360 --> 00:02:42,400
 So, I just given a random session ID here, 2, 2, 6, 5.

36
00:02:42,400 --> 00:02:48,500
 So, once the AI agent gets this request and it creates a session ID, it will reply to

37
00:02:48,500 --> 00:02:57,000
 Joe, let me check and get back and then it goes ahead and breaks down the task and maybe

38
00:02:57,000 --> 00:03:02,120
 it executes certain tools, maybe it makes a call to HR system, maybe it to the hotel booking

39
00:03:02,120 --> 00:03:03,120
 ID.

40
00:03:03,120 --> 00:03:07,240
 Now, remember, if it is going to book a hotel, it needs the dates.

41
00:03:07,240 --> 00:03:10,160
 So, here, it is talking about mid-December, 2 weeks.

42
00:03:10,160 --> 00:03:16,060
 So, all this would be stored in the session ID and then maybe passed on to these tools

43
00:03:16,060 --> 00:03:19,960
 so that they can execute based on certain parameters.

44
00:03:19,960 --> 00:03:26,000
 Now, let us say, it gets a feedback saying that no rooms are available during this duration

45
00:03:26,000 --> 00:03:28,240
 and agent lets Joe know.

46
00:03:28,240 --> 00:03:35,320
 So, maybe Joe responds with new dates and those new dates are passed on to the agent and

47
00:03:35,320 --> 00:03:38,720
 then it executes and then completes the booking.

48
00:03:38,720 --> 00:03:44,840
 But now, these new dates are also stored in the short-term memory to give these tools

49
00:03:44,840 --> 00:03:45,840
 some context.

50
00:03:45,840 --> 00:03:48,800
 So, this is how a short-term memory works.

51
00:03:48,800 --> 00:03:54,080
 So, now, if you have to just summarize it, short-term memory agents are used to store the user

52
00:03:54,080 --> 00:03:59,960
 and agent interaction and they are and most likely they are stored in a data store with

53
00:03:59,960 --> 00:04:01,920
 a particular session ID.

54
00:04:01,920 --> 00:04:06,160
 Now, let us take a quick look on how the long-term memory works.

55
00:04:06,160 --> 00:04:11,720
 Again, let us say we have Joe and we have an AI agent and let us say he interacted with

56
00:04:11,720 --> 00:04:18,640
 the agent in December 2024 and he says that in its 2 weeks vacation from mid-December

57
00:04:18,640 --> 00:04:24,040
 but he wants the hotel rooms to be non-smoking.

58
00:04:24,040 --> 00:04:29,600
 And then some interaction happens between the agent and the user and let us say this user

59
00:04:29,600 --> 00:04:34,240
 request has been fulfilled by the AI agent and the conversation ends.

60
00:04:34,240 --> 00:04:40,000
 So, once the conversation between the user and AI agent ends, then what is going to happen

61
00:04:40,000 --> 00:04:43,840
 is it is going to probably use another large language model or the same large language

62
00:04:43,840 --> 00:04:50,240
 model to summarize the interaction between the user and agent and then it is going to

63
00:04:50,240 --> 00:04:57,240
 store that in some form of data store, maybe some service in AWS, maybe a DynamoDB.

64
00:04:57,240 --> 00:05:05,680
 Now, next time when Joe comes and interacts with the agent again, maybe in June 2025 and

65
00:05:05,680 --> 00:05:08,800
 this time he wants to plan a 2-week vacation to Egypt.

66
00:05:08,800 --> 00:05:16,200
 So, what will happen is before the AI agent starts responding, it will load this interaction

67
00:05:16,200 --> 00:05:25,000
 that was stored in the data store before it responds to the new query of Joe in June 2025.

68
00:05:25,000 --> 00:05:30,680
 And how does that help, now based on the previous interaction, it already knows that Joe

69
00:05:30,680 --> 00:05:34,760
 is looking to book hotel rooms that are non-smoking.

70
00:05:34,760 --> 00:05:40,320
 So, now it has an additional content, which adds an element of personalization.

71
00:05:40,320 --> 00:05:46,400
 Now, if we just summarize the long-term memory in agents, so what are the benefits or long-term

72
00:05:46,400 --> 00:05:52,400
 memory in AI agents, if you can quickly summarize, so it provides user preference to the

73
00:05:52,400 --> 00:05:58,880
 agent based on historical interactions, then it also gives broader contextual knowledge

74
00:05:58,880 --> 00:06:05,440
 to the agent, maybe microcool employees always use Hilton hotels, so it will already know

75
00:06:05,440 --> 00:06:11,400
 that information and it will check on the site of Hilton hotels while he is booking a hotel

76
00:06:11,400 --> 00:06:13,440
 for Joe.

77
00:06:13,440 --> 00:06:19,520
 Then as we already discussed, it summarizes all the interactions and stores in a data store

78
00:06:19,520 --> 00:06:26,520
 and this could be between 1 to 365 days and when a new interaction happens, all these

79
00:06:26,520 --> 00:06:29,440
 summarized interactions are loaded.

80
00:06:29,440 --> 00:06:33,520
 Okay, that is pretty much it from this lecture, I will see you in the next lecture.

81
00:06:33,520 --> 00:06:33,960
 Thank you.

